  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"61\" data-end=\"287\">The <strong data-start=\"65\" data-end=\"95\">Platelet-Rich Plasma (PRP)</strong> test is not a diagnostic test like most blood tests but rather a <strong data-start=\"161\" data-end=\"188\">therapeutic preparation</strong> used in <strong data-start=\"197\" data-end=\"222\">regenerative medicine</strong>, <strong data-start=\"224\" data-end=\"239\">orthopedics</strong>, <strong data-start=\"241\" data-end=\"256\">dermatology</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"262\" data-end=\"286\">aesthetic treatments</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"289\" data-end=\"464\">However, when <strong data-start=\"303\" data-end=\"356\">lab values or platelet counts in PRP preparations</strong> are reported, the interpretation is about the <strong data-start=\"403\" data-end=\"445\">quality and concentration of platelets</strong> in the PRP sample.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1719\" data-end=\"1749\">Role of Platelets in PRP</p>\n<p data-start=\"1751\" data-end=\"1793\">Platelets release <strong data-start=\"1769\" data-end=\"1787\">growth factors</strong> like:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1794\" data-end=\"1904\">\n<li data-start=\"1794\" data-end=\"1837\">\n<p data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1837\"><strong data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1804\">PDGF</strong> (Platelet-Derived Growth Factor)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1838\" data-end=\"1878\">\n<p data-start=\"1840\" data-end=\"1878\"><strong data-start=\"1840\" data-end=\"1849\">TGF-&beta;</strong> (Transforming Growth Factor)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1879\" data-end=\"1904\">\n<p data-start=\"1881\" data-end=\"1904\"><strong data-start=\"1881\" data-end=\"1889\">VEGF</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1891\" data-end=\"1898\">EGF</strong>, etc.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1906\" data-end=\"1920\">These promote:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1921\" data-end=\"2031\">\n<li data-start=\"1921\" data-end=\"1940\">\n<p data-start=\"1923\" data-end=\"1940\"><strong data-start=\"1923\" data-end=\"1940\">Tissue repair</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1941\" data-end=\"1965\">\n<p data-start=\"1943\" data-end=\"1965\"><strong data-start=\"1943\" data-end=\"1965\">Collagen formation</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1966\" data-end=\"1984\">\n<p data-start=\"1968\" data-end=\"1984\"><strong data-start=\"1968\" data-end=\"1984\">Angiogenesis</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1985\" data-end=\"2004\">\n<p data-start=\"1987\" data-end=\"2004\"><strong data-start=\"1987\" data-end=\"2004\">Hair regrowth</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2005\" data-end=\"2031\">\n<p data-start=\"2007\" data-end=\"2031\"><strong data-start=\"2007\" data-end=\"2031\">Joint/tendon healing</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Component</th>\n<th>What It Means</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High PRP platelet count</strong></td>\n<td>Good-quality PRP : likely to be therapeutically effective</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low PRP platelet count</strong></td>\n<td>Poor concentration : may not give desired clinical results</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>No count provided</strong></td>\n<td>Depends on technique used; difficult to verify quality without measurement</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
